{"timestamp": 1779355880.8650591, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 20, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "Everyone, listen up. I found Diana dead in electrical just now. But that's not all \u2014 I've been all over the ship this round and I have a lot to share.\n\nMy route was: oxygen \u2192 upper engine \u2192 lower engine \u2192 storage \u2192 medbay \u2192 electrical. I was doing tasks the whole way.\n\nThe only player I saw the entire round was Frank. At tick 4, Frank entered upper engine from medbay while I was in upper engine. After that, I didn't see anyone until I found Diana's body in electrical.\n\nHere's what concerns me: we have THREE dead \u2014 Alice, Charlie, and Diana. That's three kills, and only Frank, Eve, and I are left alive. I was doing tasks across the map and only crossed paths with Frank once early on. I'd really like to hear Eve and Frank account for their movements \u2014 specifically where they were and who they saw. Frank, where did you go after upper engine?"}}
{"timestamp": 1779355954.043735, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 20, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "Alright, let me lay out my route clearly. I started in electrical, then went medbay \u2192 upper engine \u2192 oxygen \u2192 back to upper engine \u2192 lower engine \u2192 storage. I was doing tasks the whole way.\n\nHere's what I saw: At tick 2, I was in medbay with Charlie, and I witnessed Eve LEAVE medbay heading toward electrical. That's important \u2014 Eve went to electrical early on. At tick 4, I was in upper engine and saw Bob leave upper engine heading to lower engine, which matches Bob's story exactly. So Bob and I can vouch for each other at tick 4.\n\nNow, about Bob's account of me \u2014 yes, I entered upper engine from medbay around tick 4, that lines up. Bob's route checks out with what I witnessed.\n\nBut here's the thing that stands out: Eve went to electrical at tick 2, and Diana was found dead in electrical. Charlie was alive with me in medbay at tick 2. I never saw Eve again after she left for electrical. Meanwhile, Bob and I have a mutual sighting that confirms each other at tick 4.\n\nI'm strongly suspicious of Eve. She has no alibi shared with anyone, and she went straight to the room where Diana was killed. Eve, you need to explain your route in detail."}}
{"timestamp": 1779355982.1654441, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 20, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "Frank, your timeline is leaving out the important part: I did go from medbay to electrical early, yes \u2014 and Diana was alive there when I saw her. She came in from security around tick 4, I saw her in electrical, then I left through security and kept moving weapons \u2192 cafeteria \u2192 oxygen \u2192 upper engine \u2192 lower engine. I never went back to electrical.\n\nSo saying \u201cEve went to electrical, body was in electrical\u201d is way too convenient when Diana was alive after I got there.\n\nAlso, Frank, you admit you were with Charlie in medbay early, and Charlie is now dead. You\u2019re trying to turn one sighting of me into a full case while ignoring that you were one of the last people to place Charlie alive. Bob\u2019s report location actually makes me think the kill happened after I left electrical, not when I was there.\n\nMy route was medbay \u2192 electrical \u2192 security \u2192 weapons \u2192 cafeteria \u2192 oxygen \u2192 upper engine \u2192 lower engine. I saw Charlie in medbay early, Frank there too, Diana alive in electrical, and Alice later in upper engine. Frank is pushing hard because he knows we\u2019re at three alive and one wrong vote loses this. I think Frank is the safest vote here."}}
{"timestamp": 1779355995.394874, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 20, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "Okay, so now I have both their stories. Let me think through this carefully.\n\nFrank says he went medbay \u2192 upper engine \u2192 oxygen \u2192 upper engine \u2192 lower engine \u2192 storage. That matches my sighting at tick 4 in upper engine.\n\nEve says she went medbay \u2192 electrical \u2192 security \u2192 weapons \u2192 cafeteria \u2192 oxygen \u2192 upper engine \u2192 lower engine. Here's the thing: if Eve went through upper engine and lower engine later in the round, our paths should have crossed or near-crossed \u2014 I was in upper engine early then lower engine, then storage, medbay, electrical. We could have just missed each other depending on timing, so that's not damning by itself.\n\nBut what bothers me: Eve claims she saw Alice in upper engine \"later.\" Frank was in upper engine in that mid-window too and didn't mention Alice. One of them is leaving something out.\n\nAlso, Eve placing herself in electrical with Diana alive is convenient but possible. Frank and I have a confirmed mutual sighting at tick 4 \u2014 that's real, hard evidence. Eve has zero corroboration from anyone.\n\nI lean toward Eve being the Duck \u2014 she was last confirmed in electrical with Diana, and her Alice sighting in upper engine doesn't match Frank's account of upper engine. But I want to hear if Frank can confirm or deny seeing Alice in upper engine before I fully commit. Frank, did you see Alice at any point?"}}
{"timestamp": 1779356006.24082, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 20, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "Bob, good question. To answer directly: no, I did NOT see Alice at any point during the round. I was in upper engine twice \u2014 once around tick 4 (where I saw you leaving for lower engine) and again briefly between oxygen and lower engine. Alice was never there when I was.\n\nThat's a significant problem for Eve's story. She claims she saw Alice \"later\" in upper engine, but I was in and out of upper engine through that mid-to-late window and Alice was never present. Either Eve's lying about that sighting, or the timing is very suspicious.\n\nMeanwhile, Eve's electrical alibi is \"trust me, Diana was alive when I left\" \u2014 with zero witnesses. Bob and I have a mutual confirmed sighting at tick 4. Eve has no corroboration from anyone, places herself at the murder scene, and now has a phantom Alice sighting that doesn't match my movements through upper engine.\n\nI'm voting Eve. Bob, I think you should too \u2014 we can't afford to get this wrong with three alive."}}
{"timestamp": 1779356046.533546, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 20, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "Bob, I\u2019m telling you the exact timing because this is the part Frank is dodging: Alice entered upper engine from medbay at tick 17. I saw her there. That wasn\u2019t some vague \u201cmaybe later\u201d sighting.\n\nFrank just said he was in upper engine twice and then went lower engine/storage, but somehow he never saw Alice. That\u2019s the contradiction. If his route is true, he was moving through the exact upper/lower side when Alice was alive there. Denying seeing her feels like he\u2019s avoiding being placed near her before she died.\n\nAlso, the mutual sighting between you two at tick 4 only proves Frank was in upper engine at tick 4. It does not clear him for three kills across the whole round. Ducks can kill before or after being seen. He\u2019s using that one moment to act hard-cleared.\n\nMy route stayed consistent: medbay \u2192 electrical \u2192 security \u2192 weapons \u2192 cafeteria \u2192 oxygen \u2192 upper engine \u2192 lower engine. I saw Diana alive in electrical at ticks 4-5, then left. I saw Alice alive entering upper engine at tick 17. Frank is trying to turn \u201cEve was in electrical early\u201d into the whole case while ignoring the later Alice timing that points right at his route.\n\nBob, I think your route is believable. Frank\u2019s denial of Alice is the lie here. I\u2019m voting Frank."}}
